# =============================================================================
# DD2 Website Platform — environment contract
# =============================================================================
# Copy to `.env` for local development. NEVER commit `.env`.
# In every deployed environment these live in the platform secret store, never in
# the repository (`09` §1). Rotate on schedule and CALENDAR THE EXPIRY DATES —
# silent secret expiry is the most common avoidable outage in this stack (`09` §7).
#
# Legend:  [required]        must be set for the app to boot
#          [required@phase]  becomes required at that build phase (`05`)
#          [optional]        has a working default

# --- Core -------------------------------------------------------------------
# [required] Payload signing secret. Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
PAYLOAD_SECRET=change-me-locally-only

# [required] Postgres. Port 5433 matches docker-compose.yml, which deliberately
# avoids clashing with a system Postgres on 5432. Postgres, never Mongo (ADR-10).
DATABASE_URI=postgres://dd2:dd2_local_dev@localhost:5433/dd2

# [required] Public origin of the district apex tenant. Tenants are resolved from
# the request Host header against the `tenants` collection (`02` §4.1).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Authentication ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# CURRENT: Payload local authentication (email + password). Nothing to configure —
# create the first district-admin at /admin on an empty database.
#
# DESIGNED: Entra ID OIDC (`02` §7, ADR-6). Local auth is a deliberate, temporary
# deviation to avoid a district IT dependency during development. See "Authentication"
# in CLAUDE.md for what it costs and the switch trigger.
#
# THE GAP THAT MATTERS: local accounts have no automatic deprovisioning. A departing
# employee keeps access until someone remembers to remove them. Acceptable for
# development and a closed pilot; NOT acceptable once real school staff hold accounts.
# Switch before Phase 9 pilot cutover (`05`).
#
# THE SEEDED ADMIN. `scripts/seed.ts` creates a district-admin only when BOTH of
# these are set, and there is deliberately no default: a known credential committed
# to the repo is a standing vulnerability, and interim local auth already carries
# enough credential risk. Without them, create the first user at /admin instead.
#
# Set them if you want to run the admin-plane e2e flows (`pnpm run test:e2e:smoke`),
# which need a real session. Those specs SKIP locally when these are unset and FAIL
# in CI, where an absent session means the gate stopped covering the admin plane.
#
# The password must satisfy src/auth/password-policy.ts: 8+ characters and no banned
# fragment ("admin", "district", "dd2", "password", ...). Use a throwaway phrase and a
# `.invalid` address (RFC 2606) that can never route to a real mailbox.
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=jasonlybrand@icloud.com
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=Jack1998!

# Unset below. Populate when switching — the group -> role mapping they drive is
# already written and tested in src/auth/entra-mapping.ts.
ENTRA_TENANT_ID=
ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Entra group object IDs mapped to platform roles at login (`02` §7). Allowlist:
# an unmapped group grants nothing, and system-sync is never grantable via login.
ENTRA_GROUP_DISTRICT_ADMIN=
ENTRA_GROUP_SCHOOL_MANAGER=

# --- Object storage: Cloudflare R2 ------------------------------ [required@6] -
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=
R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# --- Cache invalidation: Cloudflare ----------------------------- [required@2] -
# Publish -> on-demand revalidate + targeted tag purge (`02` §5, `09` §4.2).
REVALIDATION_SECRET=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# --- Translation: Azure AI Translator --------------------------- [required@7] -
# Engine is swappable; the pipeline depends on an interface, not on Azure (`08` §4).
AZURE_TRANSLATOR_KEY=
AZURE_TRANSLATOR_REGION=
AZURE_TRANSLATOR_ENDPOINT=

# --- Transactional email: Resend -------------------------------- [required@4] -
# Approval notifications and system alerts ONLY. Mass communication is out of
# scope and runs on a separate district service (`01` §5).
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=

# --- PowerSchool staff sync ------------------------------------- [required@5] -
# READ-ONLY, staff-scoped credential. Provision with the narrowest data access the
# district can grant — ideally scoped so student endpoints are not even reachable
# by the token (`11` §2, §8). NO STUDENT DATA, EVER.
POWERSCHOOL_BASE_URL=
POWERSCHOOL_CLIENT_ID=
POWERSCHOOL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Observability ---------------------------------------------- [optional] ---
SENTRY_DSN=
